{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "start": 2.2,
      "end": 4.1,
      "text": "The bay is wide and the water is grey,"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.6,
      "end": 6.4,
      "text": "and the boats are small and far away."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.0,
      "end": 9.2,
      "text": "I climb the cliff with the wind in my coat,"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.7,
      "end": 11.6,
      "text": "counting the steps I have walked by the note."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.0,
      "end": 52.8,
      "text": "The harbour hums with an iron chain,"
    },
    {
      "start": 53.3,
      "end": 55.2,
      "text": "and the gulls cry out the weather's refrain."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.8,
      "end": 58.1,
      "text": "The storm comes up like a wall of glass,"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.6,
      "end": 60.4,
      "text": "and every lamp in the town goes dark as it passes."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.0,
      "end": 62.8,
      "text": "And I light the lantern, I light it again,"
    },
    {
      "start": 63.2,
      "end": 65.0,
      "text": "I light it for the boats and for the rain."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.6,
      "end": 67.7,
      "text": "Turn my face to the weather, turn my face to the sea,"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.2,
      "end": 70.0,
      "text": "keep a light on the headland and a light on me."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.0,
      "end": 62.8,
      "text": "And I light the lantern, I light it again,"
    },
    {
